 r←GetNewestPerMajor registryPath;list;majors;lastOfEach
⍝ Returns the package IDs of the newest release in every major version line.
⍝ That is exactly the set a README is ever wanted for: only the newest release of a line is
⍝ rendered, so fetching anything else would be work nobody looks at.
⍝ "Newest" is Tatin's order, which `Reg.GetAllPackages` delivers already: by version number
⍝ and, where that cannot decide, as with betas, by publishing date, the best one last. The
⍝ package page picks its release the same way, so it looks for a README where one was stored.
 list←,Reg.GetAllPackages registryPath
 majors←Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨list
 lastOfEach←(1+≢majors)-(⌽majors)⍳∪majors
 r←list[lastOfEach]
